From 28705eef10a2854b898ae5ca240a47dac2abdcd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:45:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 341/371] family server: a pirate in a guild can log out
 without being dropped (109, "lost connection")

GuildManager.handleLogout ran cr.removeAIInterest(AIInterestHandles.PIRATES_GUILD) for every pirate in a guild
when the client sent StopVisibilityEvent at logout. Panda's DoInterestManager._sendRemoveAIInterest writes the old
OTP CLIENT_REMOVE_INTEREST (uint16 (1<<15)+handle, no context; it has no Astron branch, unlike _sendRemoveInterest).
Astron reads uint32 context + uint16 interest id, so the 4-byte message is a truncated datagram and it ejects the
client with 109 "Datagram unexpectedly ended". games' LIVE-relog caught the bytes (payload 0380) on claude2 after it
joined a guild; on land and on a ship alike.

Nothing on this server opens AI interest PIRATES_GUILD, so handleLogout now sends nothing; the accept stays. Client
file (the AI loads it through PCGuildManager but handleLogout only runs on the client): client patch 43, no restart.
test_guild_logout.py (real GuildManager on Panda's real DoInterestManager, every sent message checked against
Astron's minimum length): client tree FAIL (type 203, 2 bytes after the type), fixed file PASS (0 sent).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 otp/friends/GuildManager.py | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/otp/friends/GuildManager.py b/otp/friends/GuildManager.py
index fd7c0b9..9577982 100644
--- a/otp/friends/GuildManager.py
+++ b/otp/friends/GuildManager.py
@@ -400,5 +400,9 @@ class GuildManager(DistributedObjectGlobal):
 
     @report(types=['args'], dConfigParam='want-guildmgr-report')
     def handleLogout(self, *args, **kw):
-        self.cr.removeAIInterest(AIInterestHandles.PIRATES_GUILD)
+        # family server (2026-11-21): send nothing. removeAIInterest builds the old OTP CLIENT_REMOVE_INTEREST (the
+        # handle alone, no context); Astron reads it as a truncated datagram and drops the client (109, 'lost
+        # connection') every time a guild member logs out. Nothing on this server opens AI interest PIRATES_GUILD,
+        # so there is nothing to close.
+        pass
 
